2:T11cf,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","headline":"IPTV Buffering, Freezing and Lag: How to Fix It","description":"Why IPTV buffers in the UK and how to fix it. Work out whether the problem is your Wi-Fi, your device, ISP throttling on BT, Sky, Virgin or TalkTalk, or the provider — with the fix for each.","image":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/images/guides/iptv-buffering-fix.svg","dateModified":"2026-08-14","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-buffering-fix-uk","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-buffering-fix-uk","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"IPTV UK","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/icon.svg"}},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"IPTV UK","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/icon.svg"}}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does my IPTV keep buffering in the evening?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Evening buffering that clears overnight is nearly always congestion or ISP traffic shaping rather than the service itself. Test the same channel on mobile data during a bad spell: if it plays cleanly there, the problem is your broadband connection or your ISP, and a wired connection followed by a DNS change are the two fixes worth trying first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will a VPN stop IPTV buffering?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only if your ISP is shaping or blocking the traffic. A VPN hides what you are streaming, so it defeats throttling — but it cannot create bandwidth, so it does nothing for weak Wi-Fi, a slow device or genuine congestion, and a free VPN will usually make things worse. Trial one for a single evening and judge it immediately."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is my ISP blocking IPTV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is possible. UK ISPs including BT, Sky, Virgin Media and TalkTalk have come under growing pressure to restrict streaming traffic. The signature is a speed test that reports your full line rate while the stream still stutters, or a player that cannot connect at all. Changing to a public DNS resolver is the first thing to try, because it is free and takes two minutes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much broadband speed do I need for IPTV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Roughly 5 Mbps for standard definition, 10 Mbps for HD and 25 Mbps for 4K — per stream, so two televisions watching at once need both. Steadiness matters more than the headline number: a stable 20 Mbps connection outperforms a 200 Mbps one that drops every few minutes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does only one channel buffer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is the source feed rather than anything at your end, and no change to your network or device will fix it. Send us the channel name and we will get it restored."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Ethernet really make that much difference?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — it is consistently the single most effective change. Televisions have weaker aerials than the phone sitting next to them, and Wi-Fi contends with walls, neighbours and every other device in the house. A cable removes all of that at once, and for live sport it is the difference most people notice immediately."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"My IPTV worked fine and suddenly started buffering. What changed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The usual culprits are a full device, an accumulated programme guide cache, a system update that reset network settings, or a new device on your home network competing for bandwidth. Clear the player cache, restart at the plug rather than standby, and check what else has joined the Wi-Fi recently."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I switch provider if it keeps buffering?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not before you have run the mobile-data test. If the stream buffers on mobile data as well as broadband, changing provider might help. If it plays cleanly on mobile data, the problem is on your side of the front door and a new subscription will behave exactly the same way."}}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Guides","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/guides"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"IPTV Buffering Fix UK","item":"https://www.iptvuk.buzz/iptv-buffering-fix-uk"}]}]}6:["guideSlug","iptv-buffering-fix-uk","d"]
0:["gmjwm0ccykok87_eKU8cA",[[["",{"children":[["guideSlug","iptv-buffering-fix-uk","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"guideSlug\":\"iptv-buffering-fix-uk\"}",{}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":[["guideSlug","iptv-buffering-fix-uk","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",["$","main",null,{"className":"bg-white text-slate-900","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","$L3",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"bg-white","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"relative overflow-hidden bg-slate-950 text-white","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_top_left,_rgba(249,115,22,0.25),_transparent_45%),radial-gradient(circle_at_bottom_right,_rgba(14,165,233,0.2),_transparent_45%)]"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-16","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-400","children":[["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/","className":"transition hover:text-orange-300","children":"Home"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mx-2 text-slate-600","children":"/"}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/guides","className":"transition hover:text-orange-300","children":"Guides"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mx-2 text-slate-600","children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-slate-300","children":"Troubleshooting"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex rounded-full border border-orange-400/30 bg-orange-500/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-orange-200","children":"Troubleshooting"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl","children":"IPTV Buffering, Freezing and Lag: How to Fix It"}],[["$","p","Almost every IPTV buffering complaint ha",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-slate-300 sm:text-lg","children":"Almost every IPTV buffering complaint has one of four causes: the network path to your television, the device doing the decoding, your ISP shaping the traffic, or the provider’s server. They produce very similar symptoms and completely different fixes, which is why swapping provider often changes nothing."}],["$","p","This guide is ordered so you can identif",{"className":"mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-slate-300 sm:text-lg","children":"This guide is ordered so you can identify which one you have before changing anything. Work through it in order and most people find the answer within the first two sections."}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-400","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"11 min read"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-slate-600","children":"•"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Updated ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-08-14","children":"14 August 2026"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2","children":[["$","span","Five-minute diagnosis",{"className":"rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white/90","children":"Five-minute diagnosis"}],["$","span","Fixes ranked by effect",{"className":"rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white/90","children":"Fixes ranked by effect"}],["$","span","When a VPN helps and when it does not",{"className":"rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-white/90","children":"When a VPN helps and when it does not"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-hidden rounded-[1.75rem] border border-white/10 bg-white/5 shadow-[0_35px_100px_-45px_rgba(0,0,0,0.9)]","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/images/guides/iptv-buffering-fix.svg","alt":"A live stream stalling on a buffering wheel next to a network diagnostic panel","width":1200,"height":630,"className":"h-auto w-full","fetchPriority":"high"}]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-16","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_270px] lg:gap-14","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0","children":[[["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"Buffering is what happens when your player runs out of video before the next piece arrives. It is always a supply problem. The useful question is not \"why is it buffering\" but \"where in the chain did the supply break\", and that chain has four links: the provider’s server, your ISP, your home network, and the device itself."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"diagnose","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Diagnose It First: A Five-Minute Test"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"Do not change any settings yet. These four checks tell you which link is failing, and each one takes about a minute."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"mt-6 space-y-4","children":[["$","li","Does it buffer on one channel or all of them?",{"className":"flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-4 sm:px-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-xs font-bold text-white","children":1}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-base","children":"Does it buffer on one channel or all of them?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 mt-1","children":"If one channel stutters while everything else is fine, that is the source feed, not your setup. Nothing you change at home will fix it — send us the channel name instead. If every channel buffers, carry on down this list."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Does it buffer on mobile data?",{"className":"flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-4 sm:px-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-xs font-bold text-white","children":2}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-base","children":"Does it buffer on mobile data?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 mt-1","children":"Tether your phone to the device, or play the same channel on your phone using 4G or 5G with Wi-Fi off. If it plays cleanly on mobile data but not on your broadband, the problem is your home network or your ISP. If it buffers on both, it is the provider’s server or your device."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Does it buffer on a second device?",{"className":"flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-4 sm:px-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-xs font-bold text-white","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-base","children":"Does it buffer on a second device?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 mt-1","children":"Play the same channel on a laptop or phone sitting next to the television, on the same Wi-Fi. If the laptop is fine and the television is not, the television or the streaming stick is the bottleneck, not your connection."}]]}]]}],["$","li","Does it buffer at the same time every evening?",{"className":"flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-4 py-4 sm:px-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-900 text-xs font-bold text-white","children":4}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-base","children":"Does it buffer at the same time every evening?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 mt-1","children":"Trouble that appears reliably between about 7pm and 11pm and disappears overnight points at congestion — either your ISP’s local capacity or traffic shaping. Trouble that is constant regardless of time points at your setup."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border px-5 py-4 border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-950","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] opacity-70","children":"The single most useful result"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 mt-2","children":"The mobile-data test is the one that saves the most time. It cleanly separates \"everything before my front door\" from \"everything after it\", and that split determines which half of this guide you need."}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"network","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Fix 1: Your Home Network (Most Common by Far)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"If the mobile-data test played cleanly, the problem is between your router and your screen. This is where the overwhelming majority of buffering actually lives, and it is also the cheapest to fix."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","article","Run an Ethernet cable",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-45px_rgba(15,23,42,0.5)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start justify-between gap-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-bold text-slate-900","children":"Run an Ethernet cable"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 rounded-full bg-orange-50 px-3 py-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-orange-600","children":"Biggest effect"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"One cable from the router to the television or box removes every Wi-Fi variable at once — interference, distance, walls, neighbours, and the weak aerials most televisions ship with. If you fix one thing, fix this. A twenty-metre flat cable costs less than a month of most subscriptions."}]]}],["$","article","Move to the 5 GHz band",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-45px_rgba(15,23,42,0.5)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start justify-between gap-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-bold text-slate-900","children":"Move to the 5 GHz band"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Most routers broadcast two networks. The 2.4 GHz one travels further but is slower and shares space with every microwave and baby monitor on the street. If your device supports 5 GHz, connect it to that network specifically rather than letting it choose."}]]}],["$","article","Check what else is running",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-45px_rgba(15,23,42,0.5)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start justify-between gap-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-bold text-slate-900","children":"Check what else is running"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"A game console downloading an update, a phone backing up photos, or another television streaming 4K will all take priority you did not intend to give them. Pause the big downloads and see whether the picture settles."}]]}],["$","article","Move the router, not the TV",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-45px_rgba(15,23,42,0.5)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start justify-between gap-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-bold text-slate-900","children":"Move the router, not the TV"}],null]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Routers hidden in cupboards, behind televisions or on the floor lose a surprising amount of signal. Out in the open and higher up is a free improvement. A powerline adapter or mesh node is the next step if the room is genuinely too far away."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":["Our ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/installation-guide","className":"font-semibold text-orange-600 underline decoration-orange-300 underline-offset-2 transition hover:text-orange-700","children":"device setup guide"}]," lists the bandwidth each quality tier needs — roughly 10 Mbps for HD and 25 Mbps for 4K — and those figures are per stream, so two televisions at once need both."]}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"device","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Fix 2: The Device Doing the Work"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"If a laptop plays the same channel cleanly on the same Wi-Fi, your streaming device is the bottleneck. Sticks and cheaper boxes have very little storage and memory, and both fill up quietly over weeks."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","Clear the player’s cache — not its data, which would remove your login",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Clear the player’s cache — not its data, which would remove your login"}]]}],["$","li","Delete apps you never open; a nearly full device stutters everywhere",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Delete apps you never open; a nearly full device stutters everywhere"}]]}],["$","li","Restart at the plug for thirty seconds rather than using standby",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Restart at the plug for thirty seconds rather than using standby"}]]}],["$","li","Close background apps, particularly on a Firestick",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Close background apps, particularly on a Firestick"}]]}],["$","li","Check for a pending system update, then restart again afterwards",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Check for a pending system update, then restart again afterwards"}]]}],["$","li","On older televisions, reinstall the player rather than updating it",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"On older televisions, reinstall the player rather than updating it"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border px-5 py-4 border-sky-200 bg-sky-50 text-sky-950","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] opacity-70","children":"Why guide data matters here"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 mt-2","children":"The electronic programme guide keeps growing as it imports more days of listings. On a device with 8 GB of storage that alone can be enough to cause stuttering after a couple of months. Clearing the cache is usually all it takes."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":["If the device is simply too old — first-generation Fire TV sticks and Smart TVs from before about 2016 are the usual suspects — no amount of clearing will fix it. The ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/best-android-tv-box-iptv-uk","className":"font-semibold text-orange-600 underline decoration-orange-300 underline-offset-2 transition hover:text-orange-700","children":"Android TV box guide"}]," covers what is worth buying, and a ",["$","$L4","3",{"href":"/iptv-firestick-subscription-uk","className":"font-semibold text-orange-600 underline decoration-orange-300 underline-offset-2 transition hover:text-orange-700","children":"Firestick"}]," remains the cheapest way to modernise an old television."]}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"isp","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Fix 3: ISP Throttling and Blocking"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"If the mobile-data test was clean and Ethernet made no difference, your ISP may be shaping the traffic. UK providers have come under increasing pressure to restrict streaming traffic, and BT, Sky, Virgin Media and TalkTalk customers report this more than most."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"Throttling and congestion look identical from the sofa. Both appear in the evening and clear overnight. The difference is that congestion affects everything — web pages feel slow too — while shaping affects the stream specifically while a speed test still reports your full line rate."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6","children":[null,["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-[0_20px_60px_-50px_rgba(15,23,42,0.6)]","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left text-sm","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-slate-900 text-white","children":[["$","th","Symptom",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em]","children":"Symptom"}],["$","th","Likely cause",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em]","children":"Likely cause"}],["$","th","What to try",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em]","children":"What to try"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","Speed test fine, stream still stutters",{"className":"bg-white","children":[["$","td","Speed test fine, stream still stutters-0",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"Speed test fine, stream still stutters"}],["$","td","Speed test fine, stream still stutters-1",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Traffic shaping"}],["$","td","Speed test fine, stream still stutters-2",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Change DNS first; a VPN if that does not help"}]]}],["$","tr","Everything slow at 8pm, fine at midnight",{"className":"bg-slate-50","children":[["$","td","Everything slow at 8pm, fine at midnight-0",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"Everything slow at 8pm, fine at midnight"}],["$","td","Everything slow at 8pm, fine at midnight-1",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Local congestion"}],["$","td","Everything slow at 8pm, fine at midnight-2",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Little you can do; a wired connection helps most"}]]}],["$","tr","Player cannot connect at all",{"className":"bg-white","children":[["$","td","Player cannot connect at all-0",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"Player cannot connect at all"}],["$","td","Player cannot connect at all-1",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"DNS-level blocking"}],["$","td","Player cannot connect at all-2",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Switch to a public DNS resolver"}]]}],["$","tr","Fine on mobile data, poor on broadband",{"className":"bg-slate-50","children":[["$","td","Fine on mobile data, poor on broadband-0",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"Fine on mobile data, poor on broadband"}],["$","td","Fine on mobile data, poor on broadband-1",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"ISP-side"}],["$","td","Fine on mobile data, poor on broadband-2",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"DNS, then VPN"}]]}],["$","tr","Poor on both",{"className":"bg-white","children":[["$","td","Poor on both-0",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":"Poor on both"}],["$","td","Poor on both-1",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Not your ISP"}],["$","td","Poor on both-2",{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 align-top leading-6 text-slate-600","children":"Go back to the device and network sections"}]]}]]}]]}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"Changing your DNS is worth trying before anything else, because it is free, takes two minutes and does not slow your connection. Some ISPs use DNS to redirect or block streaming traffic, and switching to a public resolver bypasses that entirely without needing any other software."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"vpn","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Does a VPN Fix IPTV Buffering?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"Sometimes, and it is worth being precise about when, because a VPN is widely oversold as a general fix. A VPN encrypts your traffic so your ISP cannot identify it, which means it can genuinely help with shaping and blocking. It cannot create bandwidth you do not have."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/70 p-5","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-emerald-700","children":"Pros"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-2","children":[["$","li","Defeats ISP traffic shaping aimed at streaming",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Defeats ISP traffic shaping aimed at streaming"}]]}],["$","li","Gets past DNS-level blocking of a provider’s servers",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Gets past DNS-level blocking of a provider’s servers"}]]}],["$","li","Useful if the stream is fine on mobile data but not broadband",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Useful if the stream is fine on mobile data but not broadband"}]]}],["$","li","Adds privacy on your home connection regardless",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Adds privacy on your home connection regardless"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50/70 p-5","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose-700","children":"Cons"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-2","children":[["$","li","Adds overhead, so it makes congestion-related buffering slightly worse",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-rose-500","children":"✕"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Adds overhead, so it makes congestion-related buffering slightly worse"}]]}],["$","li","Does nothing at all for weak Wi-Fi or a slow device",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-rose-500","children":"✕"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Does nothing at all for weak Wi-Fi or a slow device"}]]}],["$","li","A free VPN will almost certainly buffer more than no VPN",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-rose-500","children":"✕"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"A free VPN will almost certainly buffer more than no VPN"}]]}],["$","li","An overloaded VPN server produces the exact symptom you are trying to fix",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-rose-500","children":"✕"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"An overloaded VPN server produces the exact symptom you are trying to fix"}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 text-amber-950","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] opacity-70","children":"Test before you subscribe to anything"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-6 mt-2","children":"If a VPN is going to help, it will help immediately. Trial one, play the channel that normally stutters, and judge it that evening. If it makes no difference, the problem was never your ISP and a VPN subscription will not become useful later."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"For what it is worth, IPTV UK is designed to work without one. If you need a VPN to get a usable picture, something else in the chain is wrong and we would rather find it than have you pay for a workaround."}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"provider","className":"mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl","children":"Fix 4: When It Really Is the Provider"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600 sm:text-[17px] sm:leading-8","children":"This is the last thing to check rather than the first, but it does happen. The tell is that the trouble affects specific channels or specific times regardless of what you change, and it appears on every device in the house including on mobile data."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","One channel fails while everything else plays — that is the source feed",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"One channel fails while everything else plays — that is the source feed"}]]}],["$","li","A group of channels fails together — usually one upstream server",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"A group of channels fails together — usually one upstream server"}]]}],["$","li","Everything fails at once on every device — check the status page",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Everything fails at once on every device — check the status page"}]]}],["$","li","Quality drops during big matches but recovers afterwards — capacity",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","children":"Quality drops during big matches but recovers afterwards — capacity"}]]}],["$","li","Nothing has worked since a specific date — your line may need re-provisioning",{"className":"flex gap-3 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50/60 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 font-bold text-emerald-600","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-6","